<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 17 September, from 1111 to 1978.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1111">1111 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">915 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The child Alfonso VII is crowned king of Galicia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Galician high nobility, led by Pedro Fróilaz de Traba, crowned the child Alfonso VII king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Santiago de Compostela</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-gelmirez">Diego Gelmírez</a> anointed him. The coronation was meant to preserve his rights in Galicia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile">Alfonso VII of León and Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-gelmirez">Diego Gelmírez</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-i-komnenos" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-i-komnenos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1176">1176 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">850 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Seljuk forces ambush Manuel I Komnenos at Myriokephalon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-ii">Kilij Arslan II</a> ambushed the army of the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-i-komnenos">Manuel I Komnenos</a> in a narrow pass as it marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a>. Manuel escaped and agreed a truce, but the defeat ended Byzantine hopes of recovering central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-myriokephalon">Battle of Myriokephalon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-seljuk-wars">Byzantine–Seljuk wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1382">1382 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">644 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis the Great's daughter Mary is crowned ruler of Hungary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-of-hungary">Louis I of Hungary</a> died without a male heir, his daughter Mary was crowned with the title of &quot;King&quot; of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. She reigned until 1385 and again from 1386, while her sister Jadwiga succeeded Louis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-of-hungary">Louis I of Hungary</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1394">1394 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">632 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles VI orders the expulsion of the Jews from France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Charles VI decreed that all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> must leave the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The edict ended organised Jewish life in most of the kingdom for some four centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1462">1462 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">564 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Piotr Dunin's Polish army defeats the Teutonic Knights at Świecino</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Thirteen Years' War, Polish forces under Piotr Dunin, some 2,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a>, decisively defeated the 2,700-man army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> under Fritz Raweneck and Kaspar Nostitz. Duke Eric II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>'s auxiliaries stayed out of the battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirteen-years-war-1454-1466">Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466)</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Delegates sign the US Constitution in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thirty-nine delegates signed the Constitution, creating a federal government with separated powers and checks and balances. The Bill of Rights was added by amendment in 1791.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1862">1862 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Antietam, America's bloodiest single day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Union and Confederate armies suffered about 23,000 casualties along Antietam <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>. Lee's retreat gave Lincoln the victory he needed to announce the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emancipation-proclamation">Emancipation Proclamation</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Operation Market Garden begins in the Netherlands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 35,000 Allied airborne troops landed to seize bridges leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. The operation failed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnhem">Arnhem</a>, ending hopes of finishing the war by Christmas 1944.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1978">1978 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">48 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Israel sign the Camp David Accords</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 13 days of talks hosted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter">Jimmy Carter</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> and Menachem Begin signed two frameworks for peace. They led to the Egypt-Israel peace treaty of March 1979.</p></div></li></ol>
